<div class="container">
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>Features</h1>
    <p class="lede">Start from a Serato library or a music folder on your computer. Send selected music to your phone, make edits on either device, and review changes before publishing them back.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-lists">
    <details class="feature-list-section" open>
      <summary><span class="feature-step" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span>Start with your library</span></summary>
      <p>Cueport reads your Serato library or builds one from a music folder on your computer. Your music and library data remain local.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Serato library.</strong> Read crates, subcrates, tracks, hot cues, BPM, key, colors, comments, and beatgrid markers from your local <code>_Serato_</code> folder.</li>
        <li><strong>Cueport Direct.</strong> Open a music folder instead of linking Serato. Cueport builds a library from your files, no DJ software required.</li>
        <li><strong>Local analysis.</strong> Compute BPM, key, waveform columns, and beatgrid markers from audio on your machine.</li>
      </ul>
    </details>

    <details class="feature-list-section">
      <summary><span class="feature-step" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span>Send music to your phone</span></summary>
      <p>Pair the phone app with your computer over the local network, then send selected collections and tracks to the phone for browsing and playback.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Local playback.</strong> Play tracks from local files while browsing collections, with waveform context, cues, and beatgrid markers alongside the player.</li>
        <li><strong>Cue points and notes.</strong> Add or edit hot cues and notes whether you use Serato or Cueport Direct.</li>
        <li><strong>Phone companion.</strong> Send selected collections to the phone app, cache tracks for playback, and send phone edits back to the paired computer for review.</li>
      </ul>
    </details>

    <details class="feature-list-section">
      <summary><span class="feature-step" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span>Review before publishing</span></summary>
      <p>Cueport queues edits in a local working layer so you can review what changed before updating Serato files or keeping Cueport Direct changes in its database.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Local editing layer.</strong> Cueport marks pending edits so you can see what changed across tracks and collections.</li>
        <li><strong>Publish on approval.</strong> Serato edits write back to MP3s and crate files only when you choose to publish. Cueport Direct edits remain in their own database.</li>
        <li><strong>Backups and restore points.</strong> Cueport creates safety copies before updating Serato. Cueport Direct manages edits and restore points in a separate database.</li>
      </ul>
    </details>
  </div>

